SUBDEEP["election-night-2026-how-to-watch"]=dict(intro=f"<b>Election night is Tuesday, November 3, 2026.</b> Every House seat, 35 Senate races and 36 governor races are on the ballot. Coverage starts as early as <b>4 p.m. ET on CNN and C-SPAN</b>, and most broadcast networks go live by 7 p.m. ET, per <a href=\"{_TV}\" {EXT}>TV Insider</a>. This is a neutral viewing guide: we list every major outlet and endorse no one.",
facts=[("Date","Tue Nov 3, 2026"),("Earliest coverage","CNN and C-SPAN, 4 p.m. ET"),("Free streaming","Portions on Peacock from 5 p.m. ET; CBS News digital from 5 p.m. ET"),("Broadcast networks","ABC and CBS from 7 p.m. ET; NBC from 5 p.m. ET"),("Poll closing times","Set by each state; check yours via USA.gov"),("Results","Election night counts are unofficial until states certify")],
body=f'''<h2>Every network's start time</h2>{_ENT}<p class="by">Times from <a href="{_TV}" {EXT}>TV Insider's Oct 30 network roundup</a>. Central time is one hour earlier.</p>
<h2>Before you watch: vote first</h2><p>Polling hours and early voting rules differ by state. <a href="https://www.usa.gov/when-to-vote" {EXT}>USA.gov</a> links every state's election office. Clocks <a href="{R2}science/daylight-saving-time-ends-2026/">fall back on Sunday, Nov 1</a>, so double-check your polling place hours, and see our <a href="../early-voting-2026/">early voting guide</a>.</p>
<h2>Why results take time</h2><p>Networks and wire services project winners as votes are counted, but the numbers on screen are unofficial. States finish counting mail and provisional ballots and certify results in the days and weeks after Election Day, on their own schedules.</p>
<h2>Keep reading</h2><ul><li><a href="../elections-2026/">Elections 2026: what's on the ballot</a></li><li><a href="../government-shutdown-deadline-2026/">The Dec 11 funding deadline Congress faces next</a></li><li><a href="{R2}blog/election-night-2026-where-to-watch/">Election night in one minute</a></li><li><a href="{R2}news/november-2026-whats-coming/">Everything else coming in November</a></li></ul>'''+follow("ElectionNight"),
faq=[("What time does election night coverage start in 2026?","CNN and C-SPAN start at 4 p.m. ET on Tuesday, November 3, 2026. NBC starts at 5 p.m. ET, Fox News and MS Now at 6 p.m. ET, and ABC, CBS and NewsNation at 7 p.m. ET, per TV Insider."),("Can I stream election night for free?","Per TV Insider, portions of NBC's coverage stream on Peacock from 5 p.m. ET, and CBS News runs a show on its digital platforms from 5 p.m. ET. C-SPAN carries commercial-free results."),("When do polls close on November 3, 2026?","Each state sets its own hours. Check your state election office, linked from USA.gov."),("Are election night results final?","No. Results reported on election night are unofficial. States count remaining ballots and certify results later.")])
SUBDEEP["tech-stock-selloff-oct-30-2026"]=dict(intro=f"<b>Tech stocks had a rough Friday.</b> The S&P 500 fell about 1.8% on October 30 for its worst day since June, the Nasdaq dropped 2.9% and the Dow lost 1.1%, the Associated Press reported (via <a href=\"{_MK}\" {EXT}>CBC News</a>). The worry: whether hundreds of billions of dollars in AI spending will pay off. Not financial advice.",
facts=[("S&P 500","About -1.8%, worst day since June"),("Nasdaq","-2.9%"),("Dow","-1.1%"),("Intel","-28.6%, its worst drop since 1974, on a weak profit forecast"),("Nvidia","-4.2%"),("Amazon","-1.4%; free cash flow of -$42.4 billion over 12 months"),("Gainers","ExxonMobil +2.2%, Chevron +1.8%, Mondelez +3.9%, Colgate-Palmolive +2.3%"),("10-year Treasury yield","4.93%")],
body=f'''<h2>What happened</h2><p>Intel led the way down after giving a fourth-quarter profit forecast below analysts' expectations. CEO Lip-Bu Tan pointed to pressure on PCs, per <a href="{_MK}" {EXT}>AP via CBC</a>. A day earlier, Alphabet fell more than 12%, its worst day on record. "We're moving out of the hopes and dreams phase of the AI trade and into the 'show me' phase," Joe Tigay of Equity Armor Investments said in a note quoted by AP.</p>
<h2>Not everything fell</h2><p>Outside tech, some big names rose, AP reported: ExxonMobil gained 2.2%, Chevron 1.8%, Mondelez 3.9% and Colgate-Palmolive 2.3%. Crypto stocks tumbled after a hack at Binance, the world's biggest crypto exchange, and bitcoin fell toward $77,000.</p>
<p class="warn">Not financial advice. Information only. Prices move fast; check the linked source and talk to a licensed professional about your own situation.</p>
<h2>Keep reading</h2><ul><li><a href="../big-tech-earnings-fed-week-oct-2026/">Big Tech earnings: Alphabet, Amazon, Intel</a></li><li><a href="../fed-decision-october-2026/">The Fed's Oct 28 hold</a></li><li><a href="../trending-stocks/">Trending stocks</a></li><li><a href="{R2}money/2027-tax-numbers/">2027 tax numbers tracker</a></li></ul>'''+follow("StockMarket"),
faq=[("Why did tech stocks fall on October 30, 2026?","Worries that massive AI spending won't pay off quickly, plus Intel's weak forecast, per AP. Intel fell 28.6% and Nvidia 4.2%."),("How much did the S&P 500 fall on October 30, 2026?","About 1.8%, its worst day since June. The Nasdaq fell 2.9% and the Dow 1.1%."),("Is this financial advice?","No. This page explains news coverage and is information only.")])
