# --- WNBA Game 7: tonight ---
_g7=SUBDEEP["wnba-finals-game-7-2026"]
_g7["intro"]="<b>Game 7 is tonight.</b> The Atlanta Dream and Golden State Valkyries play for the 2026 WNBA title on <b>Saturday, October 31, at 8 p.m. ET (5 p.m. PT; midnight GMT) at Chase Center</b> in San Francisco, on USA and Peacock, with coverage starting at 7 p.m. ET, per NBC Sports. It's the first Game 7 in WNBA Finals history, and either way a franchise wins its first championship. We'll add the result after the game."
_g7["facts"]=[("Tip-off","Tonight, Sat Oct 31, 8 p.m. ET (5 p.m. PT)"),("Coverage starts","7 p.m. ET (NBC Sports)"),("Stream","Peacock"),("Where","Chase Center, San Francisco"),("Series","Tied 3-3"),("First title","Neither team has won one; Golden State is in its second season")]+[f for f in _g7["facts"] if f[0] not in("Series","Where","Stream","TV","Tip-off")]
_g7["body"]=f'''<h2>What decides it</h2><p>In this series, the Dream have lost every game in which they scored under 70 and won every game in which they reached 70, per <a href="https://www.espn.com/wnba/story/_/id/50324250/finals-2026-game-7-preview-atlanta-valkyries" {EXT}>ESPN</a>. WNBA.com notes Allisha Gray played Game 6 through two dislocated fingers on her shooting hand and shot 8 of 12, including 5 of 7 from three, per its <a href="https://www.wnba.com/game/atl-vs-gsv-1042600307" {EXT}>Game 7 preview</a>.</p>
<h2>How to watch</h2><p>USA has the game at 8 p.m. ET, coverage starts at 7 p.m. ET, and Peacock streams it, per <a href="https://www.nbcsports.com/wnba/news/how-to-watch-atlanta-dream-vs-golden-state-valkyries-tv-live-stream-for-wnba-finals-game-7" {EXT}>NBC Sports</a>. The Dream have reached the Finals in 2010, 2011, 2013 and 2026 without a title.</p>
<h2>How Atlanta forced it</h2><p>The Dream won Game 6 80-69 in Atlanta and led by double digits for 33 straight minutes, by as many as 25, per WNBA.com. Golden State, the No. 2 seed, got within 77-69 with 1:15 left. Atlanta is the No. 4 seed.</p>
<h2>Keep reading</h2><ul><li><a href="../wnba-finals-2026/">Every Finals result</a></li><li><a href="{R2}blog/wnba-finals-first-game-7-2026/">The first Finals Game 7, in a minute</a></li><li><a href="{R2}pop-culture/halloween-costumes-2026/">Halloween costumes 2026</a></li><li><a href="{R2}news/november-2026-whats-coming/">What's coming in November</a></li></ul>'''+follow("WNBAFinals")
_g7["faq"]=[("What time is WNBA Finals Game 7 tonight?","8 p.m. ET (5 p.m. PT) on Saturday, October 31, 2026, at Chase Center in San Francisco. Coverage starts at 7 p.m. ET, per NBC Sports."),("What channel is WNBA Finals Game 7 on?","USA, with streaming on Peacock."),("Has either team won a WNBA title?","No. The Dream and the Valkyries are both seeking their first championship."),("Has there ever been a Game 7 in the WNBA Finals?","No. This is the first, per ESPN and WNBA.com.")]
_w=SUBDEEP["wnba-finals-2026"]
